#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:177
msgid "Subarchitecture Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:179
msgid ""
"For the ``amdgpu`` architecture the ISA version is encoded in the triple's "
"*SubArch* component. Every unique ISA has its own *minor subarch* (for "
"example ``amdgpu9.00`` for ``gfx900``). ``amdgcn`` is a legacy alias of "
"``amdgpu`` (see :ref:`amdgpu-architecture-table`) which does not support "
"subarches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:185
msgid ""
"Minor subarches are grouped into *major subarches* that name a family of "
"largely compatible ISA versions (for example ``amdgpu9``). A major subarch "
"corresponds to a :ref:`generic processor <amdgpu-generic-processor-table>` "
"when one exists for that family; the remaining major subarches are "
"placeholders for families that do not yet have a generic target for code "
"generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:192
msgid "Two subarches are considered *compatible* when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:194
msgid "they are identical, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:195
msgid ""
"one of them is the major subarch of the family that the other belongs to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:197
msgid ""
"In particular, two distinct *minor* subarches are never compatible with each "
"other, even within the same family (for example ``amdgpu9.00`` and "
"``amdgpu9.06`` are not compatible). A minor subarch is compatible with "
"itself and its own major subarch, and a major subarch is compatible with "
"itself and every minor subarch it covers. A triple with no subarch "
"(``amdgpu``) is treated as compatible with anything, as a backwards-"
"compatibility allowance. When linking modules with compatible-but-unequal "
"subarches, the more specific (minor) subarch is selected for the merged "
"module."
msgstr ""

