#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1646
msgid "Named Barriers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1648
msgid ""
"Named barriers are fixed function hardware barrier objects that are "
"available in gfx12.5+ in addition to the traditional default barriers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1651
msgid ""
"In LLVM IR, named barriers are represented by global variables of type "
"``target(\"amdgcn.named.barrier\", 0)`` in the barrier address space. "
"Programs in LLVM IR refer to named barriers using pointers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1655
msgid ""
"The following named barrier types are supported in global variables, defined "
"recursively:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1658
msgid "a single, standalone ``target(\"amdgcn.named.barrier\", 0)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1659
msgid "an array of supported types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1660
msgid "a struct containing a single element of supported type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1673
msgid "Named barrier types may not be used in ``alloca``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1675
msgid ""
"Named barriers do not have an underlying byte representation. It is "
"undefined behavior to use a pointer to any part of a named barrier object as "
"the pointer operand of a regular memory access instruction or intrinsic. "
"Pointers to named barrier objects are intended to be used with dedicated "
"intrinsics. Reading from or writing to such pointers is undefined behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1682
msgid "Strided Buffer Marker (``stridemark``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1684
msgid ""
"The strided buffer marker type ``target(\"amdgpu.stridemark\")`` is a type "
"used to allow representing the mixed index/offset access provided by buffer "
"instructions, which is used with ``ptr addrspace(9)`` - a pointer that "
"carries both indices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1688
msgid ""
"This type is a compile-time marker that has no real value and appears only "
"in element type metadata. No value of this type can be created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1691
msgid ""
"The marker type has one optional parameter - an integer indicating the "
"constant value of the stride of the buffer(s) being addressed if known. That "
"integer, if given, must be non-negative (but can be 0, indicating the "
"degenarate case where no stride is set but the index field should be used "
"anyway)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.rst:1696
msgid ""
"When creating a structured GEP, arrays of ``amdgpu.stridemark``s are used to "
"represent indexing into the *index* component of the structured/strided "
"buffer, while a subsequent bare ``getelementptr`` - is used to manipulate "
"the *offset* part."
msgstr ""

